{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14251675,"type":"Review","status":"Processing","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":6,"pointsAwarded":6,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57975,"firstName":"Harrison","lastName":"Charles","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO3yHD4gcTFRx97dYjQXmX1","sequenceId":19},"course":{"id":111,"name":"Mathematical Foundations II"},"topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-15T23:09:07.000Z","started":"2026-10-15T23:14:08.000Z","completed":"2026-10-15T23:14:57.000Z","processed":null,"progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62308705,"created":"2026-10-15T23:14:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14139,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":44930,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":14380,"text":"<p>What is the recursive formula for the following arithmetic sequence?\n\\[\n3, \\: 8, \\: 13, \\: \\ldots  \n\\]</p>\n","choice1":"$a_{n+1} = a_n + 5,\\quad a_1 = 3,\\quad n\\geq 1.$","choice2":"$a_{n+1} = a_n - 5,\\quad a_1 = 3,\\quad n\\geq 1.$","choice3":"$a_{n+1} = a_n + 5,\\quad a_1 = 1,\\quad n\\geq 1.$","choice4":"$a_{n+1} = a_n - 5,\\quad a_1 = 1,\\quad n\\geq 1.$","choice5":"$a_{n+1} = a_n + 3,\\quad a_1 = 3,\\quad n\\geq 1.$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d$ is</p>\n<p>\\[\na_{n+1} =a_n+d.\n\\]</p>\n<p>In our case, the common difference is</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*} \nd\n&=a_2-a_1 \\\\[3pt]\n&=8-3\\\\[3pt]\n&=5.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>Consequently, the recursive formula for this sequence is</p>\n<p>\\[ a_{n+1} = a_n + 5, \\quad a_1=3, \\quad n\\geq 1.\\] </p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14380,"title":"Finding a Recursive Formula"},"group":{"id":79868,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251675,"answer":{"id":62308705,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:14:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14139},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308715,"created":"2026-10-15T23:14:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12400,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":44931,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":14378,"text":"<p>What is the $5$th term of the arithmetic sequence \n\\[a_{n+1} = a_n - 5,\\quad a_1 = 3,\\quad n\\geq 1?\\]</p>\n","choice1":"$-17$","choice2":"$-22$","choice3":"$-12$","choice4":"$-27$","choice5":"$-20$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Starting with the first term $a_1=3,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $5$th term $a_5.$\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\na_1 &= 3\\\\[3pt]\na_2 &= a_1 - 5 = 3-5 = -2\\\\[3pt]\na_3 &= a_2 - 5 = -2-5 = -7 \\\\[3pt]\na_4 &= a_3 - 5 = -7-5= -12\\\\[3pt]\na_5 &= a_4 - 5 = -12-5=-17\n\\end{align}\n\\]\nTherefore, the $5$th term is $a_5=-17.$ </p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14378,"title":"Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"},"group":{"id":79860,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251675,"answer":{"id":62308715,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:14:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12400},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62308726,"created":"2026-10-15T23:14:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12973,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 11:14 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":44936,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":14378,"text":"<p>An arithmetic sequence $f(n)$ is defined by </p>\n<p>\\[\nf(n+1) = f(n) + 5,\\quad f(1) = -21,\\quad  n\\geq 1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>What is the $5$th term of the sequence?</p>\n","choice1":"$-1$","choice2":"$4$","choice3":"$9$","choice4":"$-6$","choice5":"$0$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Starting with the first term $f(1)=-21,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the $5$th term $f(5).$</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\nf(1) &= -21\\\\[3pt]\nf(2) &= f(1) + 5 = -21+5 = -16\\\\[3pt]\nf(3) &= f(2) + 5 = -16+5 = -11 \\\\[3pt]\nf(4) &= f(3) + 5 = -11+5= -6 \\\\[3pt]\nf(5) &= f(4) + 5 = -6+5= -1\n\\end{align}</p>\n<p>Therefore, the $5$th term is $f(5)=-1.$ </p>\n","topic":{"id":3695,"name":"Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"},"example":{"id":14378,"title":"Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"},"group":{"id":79862,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14251675,"answer":{"id":62308726,"cread":"2026-10-15T23:14:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12973},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}],"completedStr":"Completed on Thu, Oct 15th","localGraph":{"topicId":3695,"topics":[{"id":667,"name":"Arithmetic Sequences","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":1.8753678691057805,"repetition":2,"stability":0.20544076511140094},{"id":1226,"name":"Recursive Sequences","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":3.486787687001481,"repetition":2,"stability":0.25995461418719196},{"id":2214,"name":"Translating Between Explicit and Recursive Formulas for Arithmetic Sequences"